      "updated_at": "2026-07-27T18:53:17Z",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "The scenario where this can realistically occur is rare. And, on the other hand, silently dropping a tx because migration failed to handle a valid script would hide a real correctness bug.\r\n\r\nI wouldn't touch this, and would continue failing with a clear error that identifies the affected tx(s) so the user can act on them. I don't think dropping txs automatically and only logging the drop is the best approach, as the user may never read the log.",
